= Staal and the Free Guilds

A few months back, a line of communication was opened between the General and the Greater Worker's Guild's leadership, with the understanding of further meetings.

Following the results of the last election, Staal has reached out to the various <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> and <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> Free Guilds once again, presumably in an attempt to broker a political truce.

- @schleicher

@schleicher
title: Hear what the general has to say.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_support += 2; staal_marcher_r += 1

Greater Worker's Guild leaders Tobias Leighart and Nevin Edgemoor have met with Chancellor-designate Staal, who promised to rescind Goodryke’s most offensive emergency wage decrees, launch a public works program, and abandon the former chancellor’s plans to impose his “New State” via presidential decree. He asks only for time and quiet—a few months free of parliamentary brawling to let the state find its feet—and gives his word that he will step aside once the Commonwealth is stable again.

We are pleasantly surprised by these concessions, and Staal has earned some goodwill among the Free Guild leadership. Still, deep distrust remains—after all, he was the one controlling Goodryke when those very decrees and the unconstitutional postponement of elections were proposed.

> *"Republic or monarchy is not the question now, but rather what should this republic look like."*

 - Werner Staal